/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (Stored Cross-Site Scripting \(XSS\) is a web application vulnerability where malicious scripts are permanently stored on the target server and executed in the browsers of other users. Unlike reflected XSS, which involves user input being immediately reflected in the HTTP response, stored XSS occurs when user input is saved in a database or other persistent storage and later rendered on web pages accessed by other users.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
